WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.908
Opening DXF and CAD drawings in a browser.

2
00:00:05.408 --> 00:00:10.031
What a DXF file really contains, how to view layers and measure without

3
00:00:10.031 --> 00:00:14.133
AutoCAD, and how to turn a drawing into a PDF anyone can print.

4
00:00:15.533 --> 00:00:19.949
DWG and DXF. AutoCAD has two file formats.

5
00:00:21.249 --> 00:00:26.032
A DXF file is just text. The most common form of DXF is plain text made

6
00:00:26.032 --> 00:00:27.244
of pairs of lines.

7
00:00:28.544 --> 00:00:30.441
Converting for people without CAD.

8
00:00:30.441 --> 00:00:34.347
Most people who receive a drawing just want to look at it or print it.

9
00:00:35.647 --> 00:00:39.719
What it does not do. Drawings are often confidential: unreleased buildings,

10
00:00:39.719 --> 00:00:42.217
product designs, the layout of someone's home.

11
00:00:43.517 --> 00:00:46.008
To try it, open DXF Viewer in OpenFile.

12
00:00:46.008 --> 00:00:49.647
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

13
00:00:49.647 --> 00:00:52.904
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

14
00:00:56.617 --> 00:01:00.095
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
